1. UI (User Interface)

UI is the visual part of an application that users see and interact with.

Examples:

Buttons
Login page
Menu
Colors
Icons
Forms

Popular UI Design Tools:

Figma
Adobe XD
Sketch
2. UX (User Experience)

UX focuses on making the application easy, useful, and enjoyable to use.

UX includes:

User research
Wireframes
User flow
Navigation
Testing
Improving user satisfaction

Example:
A shopping app where users can easily search products, add them to the cart, and pay without confusion.

3. Frontend Development

Frontend is the part of the application users interact with. It converts the UI design into a working website or app.

Technologies:

HTML
CSS
JavaScript
React.js
Angular
Vue.js
Bootstrap

Responsibilities:

Build webpages
Make pages responsive
Connect with backend APIs
Add animations and interactivity
4. Backend Development

Backend handles the logic and data behind the scenes.

Responsibilities:

User authentication
Database operations
Business logic
APIs
Security
File uploads

Languages:

Python
Java
PHP
Node.js
C#
Ruby
5. Python in Backend Development

Python is one of the most popular backend programming languages.

Popular Python Frameworks:

Django
Flask
FastAPI

Python Backend Tasks:

User login and registration
Store and retrieve data
Handle payments
Create REST APIs
Connect with databases
Send emails
Generate reports

Example:
A student logs into a college portal:

Frontend shows the login form.
Python backend checks the username and password.
Database verifies the details.
Backend returns a success or failure response.
6. Database

The database stores application data.

Popular Databases:

MySQL
PostgreSQL
SQLite
MongoDB

Example Data Stored:

User accounts
Student records
Product details
Orders
Payments
7. Complete Flow
UI/UX Design
      ↓
Frontend (HTML, CSS, JavaScript, React)
      ↓
API Request
      ↓
Python Backend (Django / Flask / FastAPI)
      ↓
Database (MySQL, PostgreSQL, MongoDB)
      ↓
Response to Frontend
      ↓
Displayed to User
